:"ZInQ.pointCode, ZInQ.iota","summary":"The *code* of a point of $E(K_0)$ is the element of $\\mathbb Q^5$ \\operatorname{code}(x,y)=(0,x_0,x_1,y_0,y_1)\\quad\\text{where }x=x_0+x_1s,\\ y=y_0+y_1s,$$ with $x_0,x_1,y_0,y_1\\in\\mathbb Q$ the components of the coordinates. For $n\\in\\mathbb Z$, A *canonical code* is the code of a point of $E(K_0)$; a code of a point of $2E(K_0)$ is a code of a point of the carrier $D=2E(K_0)$.","route":"../roadmap/model/index.html#point-codes"},{"id":"model/generator","title":"The generator certificate","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.generator_certificate, ZInQ.carrierD_eq_zmultiples, ZInQ.indexEquivCarrier, ZInQ.iota_injective","summary":"The point $P_0$ has infinite order and Consequently $n\\mapsto[n]P_0$ is an isomorphism $\\mathbb Z\\to2E(K_0)=D$, the carrier $D$ is torsion-free, and $n\\mapsto\\iota(n)$ is injective.","route":"../roadmap/model/index.html#generator"},{"id":"model/membership","title":"Polynomial membership in the doubled group","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.rel_member_iff","summary":"For every $p\\in\\mathbb Q^5$, where $\\mathrm{Rel}_{\\mathtt{member}}(p)$ means that the polynomial of the membership template vanishes at $p$ and some rational values of its seven witnesses $X=(X_0,X_1)$, $Y=(Y_0,Y_1)$, $H=(H_0,H_1)$, $u$. This is an all-input statement: $p$ is an arbitrary rational $5$-tuple, not assumed to be a code.","route":"../roadmap/model/index.html#membership"},{"id":"model/membership-indices","title":"Accepted inputs have unique indices","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.rel_member_iff_iota, ZInQ.rel_member_iff_existsUnique_iota","summary":"For every $p\\in\\mathbb Q^5$, and the integer $n$ is then unique. In words, the canonical point codes form exactly the infinite cyclic group $2E(K_0)=\\mathbb ZP_0$, and the membership polynomial types arbitrary inputs.","route":"../roadmap/model/index.html#membership-indices"},{"id":"model/raw-addition-points","title":"Raw addition on canonical codes","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.rel_rawAdd_iff","summary":"For all $P,Q\\in E(K_0)$ and every $r\\in\\mathbb Q^5$, r=\\operatorname{code}(P+Q),$$ where $\\mathrm{Rel}_{\\mathtt{raw\\_add}}(p,q,r)$ means that the polynomial of the raw addition template vanishes at $(p,q,r)$ and some rational values of its six witnesses (two slope pairs $m_g,m_d$ and two inverse witnesses $u_g,u_d$). No assumption beyond $P,Q\\in E(K_0)$ is needed; two-torsion inputs are included.","route":"../roadmap/model/index.html#raw-addition-points"},{"id":"model/raw-addition","title":"Raw addition","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.rel_rawAdd_iota","summary":"For all $a,b\\in\\mathbb Z$ and every $R\\in\\mathbb Q^5$, where $\\operatorname{Add}_{\\rm raw}(p,q,r)$ is $\\mathrm{Rel}_{\\mathtt{raw\\_add}}(p,q,r)$: the polynomial of the raw addition template vanishes at $(p,q,r)$ and some rational values of its six witnesses. The branches of the template cover both identities, opposite points, distinct abscissas and doubling with nonzero ordinate. The contract concerns canonical…","route":"../roadmap/model/index.html#raw-addition"}],"result_edges":[["model/membership-indices","model/generator",0,1],["model/membership-indices","model/membership",0,1],["model/generator","model/point-codes",1,0],["model/membership","model/point-codes",1,0],["model/membership-indices","model/point-codes",1,0],["model/raw-addition","model/point-codes",1,0],["model/raw-addition-points","model/point-codes",1,0],["model/raw-addition","model/raw-addition-points",0,1]],"boundary_edges":[["model/generator","model/descent/coordinate-change",0,1],["model/generator","model/descent/mordell-weil-from-descent",0,1],["model/generator","model/descent/odd-free-index",0,1],["model/generator","model/descent/point-r-certificate",0,1],["model/generator","model/descent/rank-one",0,1],["model/generator","model/descent/torsion",0,1],["m